<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<bpmn:definitions xmlns:bpmn="http://www.omg.org/spec/BPMN/20100524/MODEL" xmlns:bpmndi="http://www.omg.org/spec/BPMN/20100524/DI" xmlns:dc="http://www.omg.org/spec/DD/20100524/DC" xmlns:di="http://www.omg.org/spec/DD/20100524/DI" id="Definitions_Process_Vendite" targetNamespace="http://corso-processi.local/apqc">
  <bpmn:process id="Process_Vendite" name="3.4.1 Develop sales forecast" isExecutable="false">
    <bpmn:documentation>Category 3.0 Market and Sell Products and Services
Process Group 3.4 Develop sales strategy (10103)
Process 3.4.1 Develop sales forecast (10129)

Definizione APQC: Developing a sales forecast for the organization's portfolio of offerings, bearing in mind the effect of promotional events, and fine-tuning these in the context of the new forecast. Estimate the future demand for the organization's products/services by analyzing historical information and any promotional activity.

Fonte: APQC PCF Cross-Industry v8.0 — Definitions and Key Measures, Category 3.0 Market and Sell Products and Services (K012576).

Documentazione completa del processo (SIPOC, matrice variabili, scheda sintetica): esempi-apqc/02-vendite/processo.md
Framework: APQC Process Classification Framework (PCF) Cross-Industry v8.0 — https://www.apqc.org/process-frameworks</bpmn:documentation>
    <bpmn:laneSet id="LaneSet_1">
      <bpmn:lane id="Lane_SA" name="Sales Analyst">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>Start</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>T1</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>T2</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>T3</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>T4</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
      </bpmn:lane>
      <bpmn:lane id="Lane_SM" name="Sales Management">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>T5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>End</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
      </bpmn:lane>
    </bpmn:laneSet>
    <bpmn:startEvent id="Start" name="Avvio ciclo di pianificazione commerciale">

      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_1</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:startEvent>
    <bpmn:task id="T1" name="3.4.1.1 Gather current and historic order information (10134)">
      <bpmn:documentation>Definizione APQC: Gathering all information about sales orders into an index. Create a directory of all sales orders, whether open or those which have been fulfilled. Track what product/service was ordered, the quantity ordered, who ordered it, the delivery date, the shipping method, the unit price and line total, payment terms, and any discount applied.

Fonte: APQC PCF Cross-Industry v8.0 — Definitions and Key Measures, Category 3.0 Market and Sell Products and Services (K012576).

Documentazione completa del processo (SIPOC, matrice variabili, scheda sintetica): esempi-apqc/02-vendite/processo.md
Framework: APQC Process Classification Framework (PCF) Cross-Industry v8.0 — https://www.apqc.org/process-frameworks</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_1</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_2</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:task>
    <bpmn:task id="T2" name="3.4.1.2 Analyze sales trends and patterns (10135)">
      <bpmn:documentation>Definizione APQC: Analyzing sales order data to identify patterns in order to capitalize on emerging trends in the industry or the economy. Identify trends among the various segments of the organization's customer base to create forecasts.

Fonte: APQC PCF Cross-Industry v8.0 — Definitions and Key Measures, Category 3.0 Market and Sell Products and Services (K012576).

Documentazione completa del processo (SIPOC, matrice variabili, scheda sintetica): esempi-apqc/02-vendite/processo.md
Framework: APQC Process Classification Framework (PCF) Cross-Industry v8.0 — https://www.apqc.org/process-frameworks</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_2</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_3</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:task>
    <bpmn:task id="T3" name="3.4.1.4 Analyze historical and planned promotions and events (10137)">
      <bpmn:documentation>Definizione APQC: Reviewing promotional activities' effect on the sales orders. Analyze all promotional events and campaigns that the organization has already employed or is planning to deploy.

Fonte: APQC PCF Cross-Industry v8.0 — Definitions and Key Measures, Category 3.0 Market and Sell Products and Services (K012576).

Documentazione completa del processo (SIPOC, matrice variabili, scheda sintetica): esempi-apqc/02-vendite/processo.md
Framework: APQC Process Classification Framework (PCF) Cross-Industry v8.0 — https://www.apqc.org/process-frameworks</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_3</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_4</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:task>
    <bpmn:task id="T4" name="3.4.1.3 Generate sales forecast (10136)">
      <bpmn:documentation>Definizione APQC: Calculating the future demand for the organization's products/services. Use the trends and patterns identified in the sales data to estimate future demand. Use forecast to prepare for future customer demand and to recalibrate the strategic course of functions and business units.

Fonte: APQC PCF Cross-Industry v8.0 — Definitions and Key Measures, Category 3.0 Market and Sell Products and Services (K012576).

Documentazione completa del processo (SIPOC, matrice variabili, scheda sintetica): esempi-apqc/02-vendite/processo.md
Framework: APQC Process Classification Framework (PCF) Cross-Industry v8.0 — https://www.apqc.org/process-frameworks</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_4</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_5</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:task>
    <bpmn:task id="T5" name="Validare la previsione (task didattico)">
      <bpmn:documentation>Task didattico: non è un'Activity del PCF. Valida la previsione con Sales Management prima della pubblicazione.

Documentazione completa del processo (SIPOC, matrice variabili, scheda sintetica): esempi-apqc/02-vendite/processo.md
Framework: APQC Process Classification Framework (PCF) Cross-Industry v8.0 — https://www.apqc.org/process-frameworks</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_5</bpmn:incoming>
      <bpmn:outgoing>Flow_6</bpmn:outgoing>
    </bpmn:task>
    <bpmn:endEvent id="End" name="Previsione approvata e distribuita">
      <bpmn:incoming>Flow_6</bpmn:incoming>

    </bpmn:endEvent>
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_1" sourceRef="Start" targetRef="T1" />
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_2" sourceRef="T1" targetRef="T2" />
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_3" sourceRef="T2" targetRef="T3" />
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_4" sourceRef="T3" targetRef="T4" />
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_5" sourceRef="T4" targetRef="T5" />
    <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="Flow_6" sourceRef="T5" targetRef="End" />
  </bpmn:process>
